  "correspondence": {
    "en": "Hamilton 1975 read the Price equation's among-group share through assortment (relatedness within groups): with groups formed by descent from uniform founders (clonal groups, the haystack limit) the within-group part vanishes and selection is among groups alone. Readings (the AI's): whether selection among groups accumulates or falls back is fixed by how the next groups are formed.",
    "zh": "Hamilton 1975 经由同类聚合（组内亲缘）读 Price 方程的组间份额：组由均匀创建者的世系形成时（克隆组、干草堆极限），组内部分消失，选择只在组间。读法（AI 的）：组间选择是积累还是回落，由下一代的组如何形成决定。"
  },
